<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Copy (245)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>copy &lt;unit&gt; &lt;dil&gt;@&lt;zone&gt;(&lt;arguments&gt;)
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>copy Papi send_prompt@update()
copy self obey@function()
</pre>
<p>Copies a DIL program onto a unit, which starts running it at once: the 
unit comes first, then the program and its arguments, as DIL's dilcopy 
takes them.
</p><p>The unit can be:
</p>
<ul><li><b>self</b> for yourself, or <b>room</b> for the room you are in;</li>
<li>a room anywhere by its symbolic name, room@zone (only rooms may be named that way);</li>
<li>someone or something here, by name.</li></ul>
<p>Things from the treasure zone are refused. You are told it was 
<i>attempted</i>: whether the program really runs depends on its name and 
arguments being right; look in the log if nothing happens. It is logged.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Zap</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Wstat</a>
</pre>




</div>